### ClearWood Furnitures — Prompt 7: storefront catalog, facets, search and the PDP
### VS Code REST Client. Runs top to bottom; @variables carry state forward.

@host = http://localhost:7180
@api = {{host}}/api/v1
@slug = kabir-3-seater-fabric-sofa

### ----------------------------------------------------------- browse

### 1. Browse Sofas — products, facets and pagination meta in one call
# @name sofas
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=sofas&limit=24

### Facet counts must be non-zero, and `pricingBasis` says which price the filters used.
@colourValueId = {{sofas.response.body.data.facets.0.values.0.value}}

### 2. Drill into Fabric Sofas — descendants of Sofas are included by the materialised path
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=fabric-sofas&limit=24

### 3. Apply a colour filter — every OTHER facet's counts should update, colour's should not
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=sofas&attributeValueIds={{colourValueId}}&limit=24

### 4. Add a price window on top (uses the indexed DEFAULT-group price)
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=sofas&attributeValueIds={{colourValueId}}&priceMin=2000000&priceMax=8000000

### 5. Sort by price, low to high
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?categorySlug=sofas&sort=PRICE_ASC&limit=10

### 6. In stock only
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?inStockOnly=true&limit=10

### 7. Cursor pagination for infinite scroll
# @name page1
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?sort=NAME_ASC&limit=12

###
GET {{api}}/catalog/products?sort=NAME_ASC&limit=12&cursor={{page1.response.body.data.nextCursor}}

### 8. Facet definitions and price bounds for a scope, with no grid attached
GET {{api}}/catalog/filters?categorySlug=sofas

### 9. Curated strips
GET {{api}}/catalog/new-arrivals?limit=8

###
GET {{api}}/catalog/best-sellers?limit=8

###
GET {{api}}/catalog/deals?limit=8

###
GET {{api}}/catalog/featured?limit=8

### 10. Category landing page: banner, children, facet defaults, featured products, SEO
GET {{api}}/catalog/categories/sofas/landing

### 11. Collections — CollectionProduct is populated by the rule evaluator, not by hand
GET {{api}}/catalog/collections

###
GET {{api}}/catalog/collections/best-sellers?limit=12

### ------------------------------------------------------------- search

### 12. Search "couch" and get sofas back — the synonym is doing the work
GET {{api}}/search?q=couch&limit=10

### 13. The same query the other way round
GET {{api}}/search?q=sofa&limit=10

### 14. A three-seater, written the way people type it
GET {{api}}/search?q=3 seater sofa&limit=10

### 15. Autocomplete
GET {{api}}/search/suggest?q=sof

### 16. Too short — expect 422 SEARCH_QUERY_TOO_SHORT
GET {{api}}/search?q=s

### 17. Injection attempt: inert, parameterised, and the table is still there
GET {{api}}/search?q=%27%3B%20DROP%20TABLE%20Product%3B%20--

### 18. Record the click that followed a search
# @name searched
GET {{api}}/search?q=sofa&limit=5

###
POST {{api}}/search/click
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queryLogId": "{{searched.response.body.data.queryLogId}}",
  "entityType": "PRODUCT",
  "entityId": "{{searched.response.body.data.products.items.0.id}}",
  "position": 0
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- PDP

### 19. The whole product page in one call, with a delivery estimate
# @name pdp
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{slug}}?pincode=400001

### The price block is the Prompt 6 PriceBreakdown verbatim — compare it with /pricing/quote.
@variantId = {{pdp.response.body.data.variants.1.id}}

### 20. Switch to another variant and watch the price move
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{slug}}?pincode=400001&variantId={{variantId}}

### 21. The same selection through the pricing engine — the totals must match exactly
POST {{api}}/pricing/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "slug": "{{slug}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "qty": 1 }],
  "pincode": "400001"
}

### 22. Option availability matrix on its own
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{slug}}/options

### 23. Related products
GET {{api}}/catalog/products/{{slug}}/related?limit=6

### 24. Recently viewed / compare: many products, one round trip
POST {{api}}/catalog/products/batch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slugs": ["kabir-3-seater-fabric-sofa", "amber-2-seater-fabric-sofa", "goli-pouffe"]
}

### 25. Record a view (rate-limited, bots ignored)
POST {{api}}/catalog/products/{{slug}}/view
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sessionId": "rest-client-session-001" }

### ------------------------------------------------------------ redirects

### 26. Resolve a live path
GET {{api}}/catalog/resolve?path=/products/{{slug}}

### 27. Rename a slug in the admin, then resolve the old one — expect a 301
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/admin/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@clearwood.local",
  "password": "ChangeMe@12345"
}

###
@csrf = {{adminLogin.response.headers.$['set-cookie'][2]}}

###
# @name product
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products?q=Veda&limit=1

###
@productId = {{product.response.body.data.0.id}}
@productVersion = {{product.response.body.data.0.version}}

### Rename it
PATCH {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "slug": "veda-armchair-renamed",
  "version": {{productVersion}}
}

### The old path now answers with a 301 to the new one
GET {{api}}/catalog/resolve?path=/veda-armchair

### 28. Junk resolves cleanly to NOT_FOUND
GET {{api}}/catalog/resolve?path=/no-such-thing

### -------------------------------------------------------------- admin

### 29. Synonyms
GET {{api}}/admin/search/synonyms?limit=50

###
POST {{api}}/admin/search/synonyms
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "term": "takht",
  "synonyms": ["diwan", "daybed", "bench"],
  "isTwoWay": true
}

### The very next search already uses it
GET {{api}}/search?q=takht&limit=5

###
DELETE {{api}}/admin/search/synonyms/takht
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 30. Reindex (chunked, returns a job)
POST {{api}}/admin/search/reindex?entityType=PRODUCT
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

###
GET {{api}}/admin/search/jobs

### 31. What shoppers searched for, and what came back empty
GET {{api}}/admin/search/analytics?days=30&limit=20

### 32. Inspect exactly what was indexed for one product
GET {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}/search-document

### 33. Dry-run a collection rule tree
POST {{api}}/admin/collections/rules/preview
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "rules": {
    "match": "ALL",
    "groups": [
      {
        "match": "ALL",
        "rules": [
          { "field": "basePricePaise", "operator": "LESS_THAN", "value": 2000000 },
          { "field": "isMadeToOrder", "operator": "EQUALS", "value": false }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limit": 20
  },
  "sampleSize": 5
}

### 34. Materialise an automatic collection
# @name collections
GET {{api}}/catalog/collections

###
POST {{api}}/admin/collections/{{collections.response.body.data.0.id}}/evaluate
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### 35. Put the renamed product back
PATCH {{api}}/admin/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "slug": "veda-armchair",
  "version": {{productVersion}}
}
